# Nexum — things that must not end up in a commit.
#
# The README has you run Nexum from the clone root with your own robot's
# config and TeamCode, so those files (and Nexum's own record) land inside
# this git working tree. None of it belongs in a repository.

# Nexum's record of YOUR robot: verified states, results, experiments —
# and .physync/gate.key, a secret that must never be committed anywhere.
.physync/
.physync-broken/

# Your robot's own files, if you copied them in here
*.xml
!app/samples/*.xml
TeamCode/
# ...but NOT the sample robot that ships with Nexum. `demo` reads it, and
# without this exception the bundled TeamCode was excluded from the published
# build: the very first command the documentation gives a team died with
# "Code directory not found". The *.xml rule above already carries the same
# exception for the same reason.
!app/samples/TeamCode/
!app/samples/TeamCode/**
YourTeamCode/
physync-robot.json
physync-stimulus.json
physync-report.md

node_modules/
.DS_Store

# Agent + editor context files. Never distributed: they carry working notes,
# internal reasoning and sometimes paths from the author's machine.
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
.cursor/
.cursorrules
.aider*
.github/copilot-instructions.md
AGENTS.md
